    "narrative": "The standout play for Ghost Ride the WHIP today is undeniably **Corbin Carroll**, boasting a commanding score of 85.94. His massive ceiling is fueled by a plus matchup against Sugano\u2019s 5.02 xERA and a high-leverage spot in the #2 hole, which maximizes his elite speed profile\u2014our most critical scarcity asset. **Tyler Soderstrom** (72.72) and **Gabriel Moreno** (71.17) also profile as elite starts, both benefiting from the same exploitable matchup against Sugano. **Brice Turang** (68.98) remains a high-floor staple in our lineup today; while he faces the respectable Walker Buehler, his leadoff placement provides a 10% boost to his efficiency, ensuring he stays active to hunt for the stolen bases that keep us competitive in the 5x5.\n\nStrategy at the margins remains focused on exploiting park factors and SP weakness, though we must navigate some difficult pitching assignments. **Mickey Moniak** (60.31) gets the start despite a platoon penalty because the matchup against the 5.81 xERA of Mitch Bratt is simply too juicy to ignore, and **Max Muncy** (63.27) gains significant leverage from a favorable park environment against Nick Martinez. Conversely, **Austin Riley** (46.88), **Jose Caballero** (46.23), and **Josh Naylor** (48.38) are on the lower end of our active spectrum due to tougher SP skill metrics and suboptimal order placement. The closest call on our bench was **Zach McKinstry**, who narrowly missed the cut with a 43.02 score; his eligibility was undercut by a poor 26-PA BvP history and a deep-lineup #9 projection, which effectively neutralized the benefits of his park factor. As a final precaution, all managers should be aware that the \"Lineup Pending\" status for **Gabriel Moreno**, **Isaac Paredes**, **Cole Young**, **Max Muncy**, **Brice Turang**, **Austin Riley**, **Seiya Suzuki**, **Mickey Moniak**, **Tyler Soderstrom**, **Corbin Carroll**, **Jose Caballero**, and **Josh Naylor** introduces non-zero risk; stay vigilant for late scratch updates, especially for our corner infielders, as we remain without the injured **James Wood** and **Giancarlo Stanton**.",
